# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/


# Added by cargo

/target
*.db
# Every example that opens a database also writes `<db>.wal`, and `*.db` does not match that.
*.wal
*.backup/

# `go build` inside cdc-consumer/ names its output after the directory, so this 60MB+ binary
# (DuckDB is linked statically) reappears every time anyone builds by hand. Named explicitly
# rather than as `cdc-consumer/*`, which would also swallow the Go sources next to it.
/cdc-consumer/cdc-consumer
# DuckDB destinations written by the tests and by the README's examples. `*.db` does not match.
*.duckdb

# The rest of a database. `*.db` matches only the heap file, and every one of these is written
# beside it: running the README's own quickstart leaves four files in a clean clone, and until this
# was added two of them showed up staged by `git add`.
#
# The copy-on-write arena's persisted free-space map, and the durable branch catalog (both added
# when the CLI was wired to the branch engine).
*.arena
*.branches
# A replica's resume position.
*.replstate
# The single-writer lock. Scoped to `*.db.lock` on purpose: a bare `*.lock` would swallow
# Cargo.lock, which is tracked and must stay that way.
*.db.lock

# Artifacts of the README's own CDC walkthrough. `out.duckdb` was already covered by `*.duckdb`,
# added for the tests, which is the only reason it was not left lying in a clean clone alongside
# these two. Verified no tracked file matches either pattern before adding them.
feed.jsonl
*.jsonl
*.sqlite

# Python bytecode from the independent wire clients in tests/pg.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Personal planning and study notes. Kept on disk, out of the repository: neither is referenced by
# any source file, test or CI step, and `plan.txt` predates the agent-isolation work entirely -
# searching all 276 lines for "branch", "agent" or "copy-on-write" returns nothing, so it reads as
# the plan for a different project than the one here.
order.txt
plan.txt
